little hope is the next game in the dark  pictures anthology series and like manna  Madden and supermassive previous hit  until dawn before it it's easy to look  at little hope and say oh it's the Salem  witch trials I got it but you'd be wrong  little hope the name of the town where  our intrepid cast find themselves is  actually based on Andover  according to supermassive games CEO Pete  Samuels the Andover witch trials are  often overlooked by the history books  but by the numbers and overs history is  the deadliest with more trials and  executions than anywhere else the Salem  witch trials as we know them were  actually split across two regions Salem  town the port city where the wealthier  families had established themselves and  Salem village where the poorer farming  families lived and worked in the year  1692 a hundred and fifty-two accusations  of witchcraft were brought forward  altogether Salem was home to 39  accusations but and over to the North  had 45 that's more than Salem town and  village combined and roughly a third of  all the witchcraft cases of 1692 the  first Andover resident to be accused was  Martha carrier who had only recently  moved to the town from Bellaire iike her  brother-in-law  Roger Toothaker was a physician back  home and he was accused of using magical  remedies his wife and daughter were  accused as well and eventually the blame  spread to Martha herself she was  executed not long after for the crime of  being related to someone who happened to  be accused and her family was far from  the only one shattered by the witch  trials  another Andover resident named Joseph  Ballard brought two girls up from Salem  to examine his sick wife Elizabeth the  girls said the cause of her illness was  witchcraft and just like that Ballard  pointed fingers and accused two local  women Mary Lacey and her daughter Mary  Jr the finger-pointing didn't stop there  Mary senior accused her own mother of  witchcraft  perhaps to deflect from herself and her  daughter but Mary jr. wound up  testifying against both her mother and  grandmother this betrayal of family this  desperation to put the attention on  someone else to save your own skin shows  the panic the people of Andover felt  it's this kind of irrationality that  intrigue  Pete's team at supermassive quote fear  was most prevalent in driving the  communities to do terrible things things  they wouldn't normally entertain the  main focus of all of our stories is  people in relationships and how those  relationships are stretched to extremes  you can witness these dynamics even in  the brief bit of little hope that we've  seen so far Andrew played by will  Poulter whom you might know from other  horror stories like black mare in  midsummer is the inquisitive type  wanting to learn more about these  horrifying events of the past in some  cases he'll even witness them in  Supernatural flashbacks the first of  these happens alongside Angela who's  much more skeptical one can imagine how  those opposing viewpoints can lead to  dramatic clashes further into the story  I definitely saw someone 100% sorry I  don't buy it  in the end nearly every accused witch in  Andover confessed and was executed only  a small few who flipped and worked for  the courts to seek out others suspected  fellow witches were spared but what  happened during the chaos leaves plenty  of room for supermassive to play around  take Arthur Miller's the crucible  possibly the most famous fictionalized  work about the Salem trials the play  does mention Andover and the trials  their only end when the people riot I'm  certainly looking forward to that sort  of dramatization with little hope the  game doesn't have a set launch date  beyond summer 2020 but keep your eye on  gamespot for more details as the release  gets closer  [Music]  you
 

